	skos:definition	"This segment includes companies that produce records, tapes, and compact discs. These companies contract with artists and arrange and finance the production of original master recordings. These companies also hold the copyright to the master recording and derive most of their revenues from the sales, leasing, and licensing of master recordings. Such companies do not have their own duplication or distribution capabilities."@en ;
